  "visualBrief": "Native Gothic civic tower with three paired lancet stages/stringcourses, actual pointed clock-arch openings and skeletal gold Roman clock rings/hands, pierced gallery tracery, four polygonal corner turrets/hourglass shutters/slate spires, thin weather poles/watchmen/gargoyles, central dormered slate spire/open gilded crown and original copper-dragon silhouette. Attached eleven-bay Cloth Hall with stepped buttresses/Gothic cross windows/blind tracery/stepped and timber dormers, corner pinnacles and south stair/gable. Small attached Mammelokker entrance with curved gable/oculus/abstract paired-figure relief. No neighboring churches/market pavilion/square/interior.",
